<Group view="presentation" inline-output="false" labelreference="L622" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Which assumptions are required for the standard MLE formulation?

A. Observations are independent
B. Observations are identically distributed
C. The model family contains the true data-generating distribution
D. The estimator must be unbiased

Correct answers: A, B, and C

Explanation:
Independence and identical distribution are required to write the likelihood as a product. MLE does not require unbiasedness and often produces biased estimators.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
