B. It simplifies differentiation
C. It changes the location of the maximum
D. It converts products into sums

Correct answers: A, B, and D

Explanation:
The log-likelihood preserves the maximum and is used for numerical and analytical convenience. It does not change the optimizer.</Text-field>
